    Bug 671497 - Fix incorrect sibling indentation when deleting messages in threaded views. r=mkmelin

    This patch resolves UI desynchronization bugs that occur when deleting
    messages in a threaded view, primarily focusing on fixing wrongly
    indented orphans and incorrect layout shifts.

    Previously, `nsMsgThreadedDBView::RemoveByIndex` manually promoted new
    thread roots and shifted children without fully updating the layout of
    the reparented siblings. Additionally, the method suffered from a deeply
    nested structure and a dead `NS_ENSURE_SUCCESS` trap that risked silent
    failures or theoretical UI glitches like undeletable ghost rows.

    Changes:
    * Fixed sibling indentation errors when a root is deleted by applying
      a native reconstruction strategy: the stale thread is collapsed, the
      newly promoted root is cleanly added via `AddHdr`, and the thread is
      natively expanded to guarantee accurate layout calculation.
    * Flattened `RemoveByIndex` using early returns to eliminate deeply
      nested `else if` chains and safely removed the dead `NS_ENSURE_SUCCESS`
      macro.
    * Added `mozilla::MakeScopeExit` guards around all array mutations to
      prevent permanent UI locks if `nsMsgDBView::RemoveByIndex` fails.
    * Extended `browser_deletionFromThreads.js` to verify correct root
      promotion and sibling indentation shifts when deleting expanded roots
      or middle-child messages.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D298697

